<https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=pcrtJZDrXrvJjH&idt=th310> a skos:Concept;
  skos:prefLabel "Manilio"@es, "Manilio"@it, "Manilius"@de, "Manilius"@en, "Manilius"@fr,
    "Manilius"@la, "Manilius"@nl;
  skos:broader <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=105814&idt=th310>, <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=pcrtK7n36RHvMy&idt=th310>;
  skos:inScheme <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/th310>;
  opentheso:memberOf <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idg=MT_1&idt=th310>;
  skos:exactMatch <http://ark.frantiq.fr/ark:/26678/pcrtJZDrXrvJjH>;
  dcterms:created "2007-02-08"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:modified "2013-05-28"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:identifier "pcrtJZDrXrvJjH";
  dcterms:description "105806##105814##pcrtJZDrXrvJjH", "105806##pcrtLG990HrK1v##pcrto2X1tJXRSS##pcrtK7n36RHvMy##pcrtJZDrXrvJjH";
  skos:scopeNote "Plin. X 4 mentions as authority regarding the phoenix a Manilius writing in the 1st. c. BCE. He cannot be identified as the Manilius author of an astronomical poem in the time of Augustus. Varro L.L. V 31 refers to a Manlius when dealing with the phoenix."@en,
    "Plin. X 4 mentions as authority regarding the phoenix a politician and writer called Manilius, writing in the 1st. c. BCE. He cannot be identified as the Manilius author of an astronomical poem in the time of Augustus. Varro L.L. V 31 refers to a Manlius when dealing with the phoenix."@fr .

