  dcterms:modified "2016-01-07"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:identifier "107664";
  dcterms:description "105780##107664", "107515##107664", "4996##4998##4999##5032##pcrtLeJDEv8jY1##107664";
  skos:scopeNote "Insect not clearly identified. Pliny considers it a sort of mosquito (culex). Leitner, Zoologische Terminologie (1972) 210, points to a double meaning of the name, designating  a sort of blood-sucking pest of horses and a little parasite of honey bees. Beavis, Insects and Other (1988), 239-240, suggests either an insect of the family of the Asilidae or perhaps a dragonfly."@fr .

