  skos:scopeNote "Plin. XI 64 considers the  cleros  as a disease that affects the hives. Arist. H.A. 605b 10 and 626b 17 makes reference to an insect called κλῆρος that destroys the honeycombs. According to Ernout, Pliny takes the cause for the effect."@fr .

