  skos:definition "Oiseau rapace diurne caractérisé par une vue perçante, un bec et des griffes en forme de faux et dressé autrefois pour la chasse. (TLFi)"@fr;
  skos:historyNote "Latin name  falco  used after Late Antiquity (4th c. onwards: Servius, Sidonius Apollinaris, Isidorus) and during the Middle Ages. Before: accipiter / ἱέραξ."@fr,
    "Name used after Late Antiquity (4th c. onwards: Servius, Sidonius Apollinaris, Isidorus) and during the Middle Ages. Before: accipiter / ἱέραξ."@la;
  skos:scopeNote "The Latin  accipiter  and the Greek  ἱέραξ  have a much wider meaning than the modern concepts of  faucon ,  halcón  or  hawk , including other kinds of birds (the cuckoo, etc.) not considered among the falcons."@fr .

