<https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108353&idt=th310> a skos:Concept;
  skos:prefLabel "cormoran"@fr, "cormorán"@es, "cormorant"@en, "mergus"@la, "αἴθυια"@gr;
  skos:related <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108655&idt=th310>;
  skos:broader <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108048&idt=th310>, <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108351&idt=th310>,
    <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=5035&idt=th310>;
  skos:inScheme <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/th310>;
  opentheso:memberOf <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idg=MT_7&idt=th310>, <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idg=MT_10&idt=th310>;
  dcterms:created "2016-02-24"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:modified "2016-02-24"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:identifier "108353";
  dcterms:description "108048##108353", "4996##4998##5000##4978##5028##pcrtqbh6Y1DsXN##5057##5059##108351##108353",
    "5037##5035##108353";
  skos:scopeNote "Lat.  mergus  and Gr. αἴθυια ,  diver , are identified as designation of diverse kinds of cormorants (so Plin. X 91). However, most probably its meaning extends to other kinds of aquatic birds. See W. G. Arnott,  Notes on gavia and mergus in latin authors, CQ LVIII, 1964, 249-262. On the identification of this bird as the cormorant in Pliny, see André, Oiseaux, 1967, 101."@fr .

