<https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108549&idt=th310> a skos:Concept;
  skos:prefLabel "caprimulgus"@la, "chotacabras"@es, "engoulevent"@fr, "goatsucker"@en,
    "αἰγοθήλας"@gr;
  skos:broader <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108187&idt=th310>, <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108547&idt=th310>,
    <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=5035&idt=th310>;
  skos:inScheme <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/th310>;
  opentheso:memberOf <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idg=MT_7&idt=th310>, <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idg=MT_10&idt=th310>;
  dcterms:created "2016-03-02"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:modified "2016-03-02"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:identifier "108549";
  dcterms:description "108187##108549", "4996##4998##5000##4978##5028##pcrtqbh6Y1DsXN##5057##5059##108547##108549",
    "5037##5035##108549";
  skos:scopeNote "The bird owes its name to the legend that it nourishes from goat milk. Nevertheless, its presence in the stables at night is to hunt the insects that are its true nourishment. On this bird, André, Oiseaux, 1967, 48."@fr .

<https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=108551&idt=th310> a skos:Concept;
  skos:prefLabel "platea"@en, "platea"@es, "platea"@fr, "platea"@la;
  skos:altLabel "platalea"@en, "platalea"@es, "platalea"@fr, "platalea"@la;
  skos:broader <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=5035&idt=th310>, <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idc=5059&idt=th310>;
  skos:inScheme <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/th310>;
  opentheso:memberOf <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idg=MT_7&idt=th310>, <https://opentheso.huma-num.fr/?idg=MT_10&idt=th310>;
  dcterms:created "2016-03-02"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:modified "2016-03-02"^^xsd:date;
  dcterms:identifier "108551";
  dcterms:description "5037##5035##108551", "4996##4998##5000##4978##5028##pcrtqbh6Y1DsXN##5057##5059##108551";
  skos:scopeNote "Plin. X 115. Bird of difficult identification. The behaviour, stealing the nourishment from other aquatic birds, leads André, Oiseaux, 1967, 132, to connect it with the genre Stercorarius. However, these birds are rare in the area of the Mediterranean (see Capponi, Ornithologia latina, 1979, 427). For other identification suggestions, as the spoonbill (Platalea leucorodia), the grey heron (Ardea cinerea) or the pelican, see André, 1967, 131-132."@fr .

